      "text": "To determine the measure of angle \\( P \\), we need to use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of a pentagon (a five-sided polygon) is \\( 540^\\circ \\). The given angles are \\( 128^\\circ \\), \\( 92^\\circ \\), \\( 113^\\circ \\), and \\( 111^\\circ \\). We can denote the unknown angle \\( P \\) as \\( x \\).\n\nThe sum of the interior angles of a pentagon can be expressed as:\n\\[\n128^\\circ + 92^\\circ + 113^\\circ + 111^\\circ + x = 540^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the given angles:\n\\[\n128 + 92 + 113 + 111 = 444\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute this sum into the equation:\n\\[\n444 + x = 540\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we solve for \\( x \\) by isolating it on one side of the equation:\n\\[\nx = 540 - 444\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 96\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of angle \\( P \\) is \\(\\boxed{96}\\).",
